{
  "AIF": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "nodeID": 1,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Ada: Governance should replace reading agent-written code as the developer's main safeguard where acceptance criteria are clear"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 2,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Ada: It keeps pace with agent velocity, because the environment enforces it on every agent run"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 3,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Ada: It also pays off in every later session, because the rules persist in the repository"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 4,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Skeptic: governance is just more agent-written code that nobody reviews and that grows without bound"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 5,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Ada: It does not grow without bound, because it needs a person's interpretation of which recurring failures reveal missing rules"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 6,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Ada: Davis et al. say agents cannot supply that interpretation"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 7,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Davis et al.: Agents' current implementation capabilities do not supply the structural interpretation needed to convert recurring failures into durable governance"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 8,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Ada: A domain with unclear acceptance criteria needs human review of agent output until its judgment calls are written down"
      },
      {
        "nodeID": 9,
        "type": "L",
        "text": "Ada: The xAIF annotation lab needs exactly that: I review each annotation the agent makes, and each correction goes into judgement-calls.md"
      },
